<article class="env-lemma" id="00NG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00NG">Lemma <span data-tag="00NG">10.104.9</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a local Noetherian Cohen-Macaulay ring of dimension $d$. Let $M$ be a finite $R$-module of depth $e$. There exists an exact complex </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to K \to F_{d-e-1} \to \ldots \to F_0 \to M \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> with each $F_ i$ finite free and $K$ maximal Cohen-Macaulay. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from the definition and Lemma <a href="/tag/00NE" data-tag="00NE">10.104.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>